<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14729" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀραχνοειδής</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰρ],
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>like a cobweb,</i> of the scum
			of urine, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιπαρότητες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Prog.</u>
					12
				</span></i>
			; also used of a <i>feeble</i> pulse, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.411
			</span></i>; of <i>capillary</i> veins, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.808
			</span></i>; of nerves, ib.<i><span class="en">
				400
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόφυσις -εστάτη</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				366
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. χιτών</span> in Medic., older
			name for the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιβληστροειδὴς χ.</span>
			(q.v.), i.e. the <i>retina,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Herophil.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Cels.
				7.7.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Onom.</u>
				153
			</span></i>; but distinguished from it by <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				10.47
			</span></i>.</div>
